+# Customer filter navigation
+
+The confirmed delay is a full document navigation after filter submit, sorting,
+paging and reset. It reloads the already verified startup data chunks. Keep the
+existing submit-to-filter behaviour and customer projection unchanged.
+
+Use a small customers-only navigator in command-center.js. It updates same-origin,
+same-path customer URLs with history.pushState, synchronizes the existing query
+object, and replaces only the current .cc-main content with customers(). Sorting,
+paging and reset links use one delegated handler. popstate rereads the URL without
+adding history. Identical URLs do not add entries. Other views, external paths,
+modified clicks, downloads and new-window links retain normal browser behaviour.
+
+No boot, authentication, execution, data loading or send path changes. Customer
+records remain memoized; ordinary full-page data refresh and the existing i18n
+MutationObserver remain in place. Targeted synthetic DOM tests cover fill versus
+submit, exact filter URLs/rows, zero fetch or reload, back/forward, duplicate
+history, sort/page/reset boundaries and unchanged data/shell nodes.
